  "description": "A hard-coded\ncryptographic key vulnerability exists in the user-configuration backup\nmechanism of TP-Link RE305 V3 and Archer C7 V5. A fixed AES-128 key and\ninitialization vector are embedded in the firmware configuration-management\ncomponent. An attacker who obtains an affected configuration backup file may\nextract the cryptographic material from the firmware and use it to decrypt the\nbackup.\u00a0\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSuccessful\nexploitation may disclose sensitive configuration information contained in a\nbackup file, including administrator passwords and Wi-Fi credentials.",
